GAMS 45.2.0  e4d2ee31 Oct 30, 2023          WEX-WEI x86 64bit/MS Windows - 12/30/25 22:34:41 Page 1
Basic CGE Model 2.0_beta2
C o m p i l a t i o n


   2   
   3  *----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   4  *This is a simple single-region, single-sector, two-factor, open-economy CGE model.
   5  *The firm maximizes its profit subjected to constant return-to-scale CES technology.
   6  *The households allocate a fixed proportion of its income as savings, which turn to investments,
   7  *and then maximize its utility (increasing & convex) subjected to the budget constraint.
   8  *The government levies a production tax & a direct tax & an import tariff, and uses income to purchase.
   9  *It operates with a constant fiscal surplus.
  10  *Imports are specified using Armington assumption, while exports follow the CET function.
  11  *In total, there are seven markets: five goods markets (activity output, exports, domestic goods,
  12  *imports, composite goods) and two factor markets.
  13  *----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  14   
